{
  "levelName": "Level 1: In The Library",
  "levelId": 1,
  "levelDescription": "Explore the library and learn fundamental Spanish greetings, introduce yourself, and help townspeople find their items.",
  "NPCS": [
    {
      "npcId": "teacher",
      "name": "Teacher",
      "talkFirstMessage": "Please talk to the Teacher by the globe first!",
      "dialogues": [
        {
          "question": "Hello! Welcome to Language Crossing. Are you ready to start learning some basic Spanish words?",
          "id": 1,
          "options": [
            {
              "optionText": "Yes, I'm ready!",
              "response": "",
              "isAnswer": true
            },
            {
              "optionText": "No, I need more time.",
              "response": "No problem! Take your time and come back when you're ready.",
              "isAnswer": false
            }
          ],
          "dictionary": []
        },
        {
          "question": "Great! Here are some things you should know first! In this first level, you will learn some basic Spanish words and phrases. To help you learn, you can use the dictionary to look up words and phrases that you unlock throughout the game. You can access the dictionary at any time by clicking on the dictionary icon in the top right corner of the screen.",
          "id": 3,
          "options": [
            {
              "optionText": "Sounds good!",
              "response": "",
              "isAnswer": true
            }
          ],
          "dictionary": []
        },
        {
          "question": "In Spanish, we conjugate verbs based on the subject of the sentence. For example, the verb 'to be' is conjugated as 'soy' for 'I am', 'eres' for 'you are', and 'es' for 'he/she/it is'. You can access the present tense conjugation cheat sheet by clicking on the cheat sheet icon in the top right corner of the screen.",
          "id": 4,
          "teaches": [
            {"spanish": "soy", "english": "I am"},
            {"spanish": "eres", "english": "you are"},
            {"spanish": "es", "english": "he/she/it is"}
          ],
          "options": [
            {
              "optionText": "Got it!",
              "response": "",
              "isAnswer": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "question": "Throughout the game, you are free to explore the world and interact with the NPCs. You can walk up to the NPCs and press E to start a conversation and learn new words and phrases.",
          "id": 5,
          "options": [
            {
              "optionText": "Thanks!",
              "response": "",
              "isAnswer": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "question": "Sometimes, NPCs will direct you to an object somewhere in the world. Find the object they describe and interact with it to help them with their task.",
          "id": 6,
          "options": [
            {
              "optionText": "Got it!",
              "response": "",
              "isAnswer": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "question": "You earn Experience Points (XP) by completing interactions and learning new words and phrases. You can track your progress with the XP bar at the bottom of the screen. Once you complete all of the interactions in a level, you will level up and unlock the next level!",
          "id": 7,
          "options": [
            {
              "optionText": "Understood!",
              "response": "",
              "isAnswer": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "question": "Now that you are familiar with the basics, are you ready to start learning some Spanish words and phrases?",
          "id": 8,
          "options": [
            {
              "optionText": "Yes, let's start!",
              "response": "Great! Head over to Sofia, our librarian, by the bookshelves. She'll teach you your first Spanish words!",
              "isAnswer": true
            },
            {
              "optionText": "No, I need more time.",
              "response": "No problem! Take your time and come back when you're ready.",
              "isAnswer": false
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
